  "practice": [
    "Say ভ three times with an extra burst of air: bhô, bhô, bhô.",
    "Practice the vowel forms: ভ, ভা, ভি, ভী, ভু, ভূ, ভে, ভৈ, ভো, and ভৌ.",
    "Hold your hand in front of your mouth and compare ব (ba) with aspirated ভ (bha).",
    "Use ভালো, ভাই, ভাত, ভয়, ভুল, ভোর, ভূত, and ভাষা as quick reading anchors."
  ],
  "notes": [
    "ভ is a Bengali consonant named bho or bhô. It is roughly an aspirated ব sound, written bh.",
    "In everyday speech, ভ can sometimes sound close to b or v depending on the speaker and word.",
    "The core ভ remains recognizable as vowel signs change around it: ভা (bha), ভি (bhi), ভী (bhi), ভু (bhu), ভূ (bhu), ভে (bhe), ভৈ (bhoi), ভো (bho), and ভৌ (bhou).",
    "ভ has an extra burst of air compared with ব. Compare বাত (bat) with ভাত (bhat), and বাল (bal) with ভাল/ভালো (bhal/bhalo)."
  ]
